{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for Tailwind CSS v4's default theme (theme.css). Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. Tailwind's palette is mode-free, so named DDD colors map straight onto it by hue; dark mode in the theme chrome pairs palette steps with light-dark(), the way dark: variants do. Tailwind has no brand color, so blue-600 stands in. Open-source values only (no Tailwind Plus/UI). Kept as DDD on purpose: duration-normal/slow and emphasized easing (Tailwind defines one transition duration), state opacities and control heights (no tokens), border widths, and heading/body sizes. Tailwind's spacing (--spacing: 0.25rem) is DDD's 4px grid. No utility classes are used in authored content.",
  "system": "tailwind",
  "title": "Tailwind",
  "prefix": "Tailwind",
  "homepage": "https://tailwindcss.com",
